 in Clay County at 5.67 inches normal, and the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids came in under 90% of normal there in 38 of 75 years since 1951. In 2025 the middle ran 48% of normal for September to October and 41% for October to November. So far in 2026 the middle shows March to April at 43% and May to June at 175%. Every grid had its driest year in 1954.</p>"}
